{"version":1784969172729,"fluff":{"BMArcher_ARC7CLaurent":{"primaryFactory":"Terra","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Earthwerks Archer"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"General Motors 350 XL"},{"label":"Armor","manufacturer":"Maximillian 100 with CASE II"},{"label":"Communications","manufacturer":"Neil 9000"},{"label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"RCA Instatrac Mark XII"}],"manufacturer":"Earthwerks-FWL, Inc."},"BMAtlas_AS7DDeathblow":{"primaryFactory":"Hesperus II,Quentin,Al Na'ir","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Foundation Type 10X"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"Vlar 300"},{"label":"Armor","manufacturer":"Durallex Special Heavy"},{"label":"Communications","manufacturer":"Angst Discom"},{"label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"Angst Accuracy"}],"manufacturer":"Defiance Industries,Independence Weaponry,Yori MechWorks"},"BMAtlas_AS7DDeathblow3045refit":{"primaryFactory":"Hesperus II,Quentin,Al Na'ir","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Foundation Type 10X"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"Vlar 300"},{"label":"Armor","manufacturer":"Durallex Special Heavy"},{"label":"Communications","manufacturer":"Angst Discom"},{"label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"Angst Accuracy"}],"manufacturer":"Defiance Industries,Independence Weaponry,Yori MechWorks"},"BMAtlas_AS7DDeathblow3059refit":{"primaryFactory":"Hesperus II,Quentin,Al Na'ir","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Foundation Type 10X"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"Vlar 300"},{"label":"Armor","manufacturer":"Durallex Special Heavy"},{"label":"Communications","manufacturer":"Angst Discom"},{"label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"Angst Accuracy"}],"manufacturer":"Defiance Industries,Independence Weaponry,Yori MechWorks"},"BMAwesome_AWS8QFatboy":{"overview":" Tasked by the SLDF to replace their aging fleet of Strikers, Technicron Manufacturing would present their Awesome in 2665. Few at the time realized that the design would quickly become one of the most coveted Assault 'Mechs of the Succession Wars to come. Nearly always tasked with the heaviest attacks, the Awesome and its PPC-based armament would come to be regarded as the quintessential \"zombie\" design. Durable, reliable, and near unstoppable, officers jump at any opportunity to field the design within their commands.","capabilities":" The PPCs of most Awesomes give it intimidating firepower over long ranges. Its thick armor plating, intelligent system placement, and lack of explosive components makes disabling one a challenging task; indeed, even flaking 'Mechs will find their attempts thwarted by the Awesome's unusually heavy rear armor. Careful heat management is a must when at the helm of an Awesome. A standard \"2-3-2\" volley became the norm for most MechWarriors, giving the 'Mech the greatest damage output without compromizing its accuracy. Its slow speed and targeting trouble with the PPCs at short range does give it some weaknesses, however, and it always fares best when well supported by a larger formation.","systems":[{"model":"Type G","label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Technicron"},{"model":"240","label":"Engine","manufacturer":"Pitban"},{"model":"Heavy Special","label":"Armor","manufacturer":"Durallex"},{"model":"T19-G","label":"Communications","manufacturer":"Garrett"},{"model":"2780","label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"Dynatec"}],"deployment":" Highly prized and used without reservation by every power of note, the Awesome is mostly concentrated in true assault formations. The manufacturing plants on Savannah were the only factories to produce the design during the Succession Wars, leading to a much greater concentration of the 'Mech within Free Worlds League space. The AWS-8Q, as the base variant of the design, was also the most produced. Even with production eventually supplanted by other variants, many AWS-8Q's would remain in general usage, with its firepower and doctrine still effective even today."},"BMBattleMaster_BLR1GHellhammer":{"primaryFactory":"Apollo,Corey,Inner Surge,Pandora,Twycross","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Hollis Mark X"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"VOX 340"},{"label":"Armor","manufacturer":"StarGuard IV"},{"label":"Communications","manufacturer":"HarfordCo COM 4000"},{"label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"HarfordCo XKZ 1"}],"manufacturer":"Diplass BattleMechs,Hollis Incorporated,Diplass BattleMechs,Red Devil Industries,Trellshire Heavy Industries"},"BMBattleMaster_BLR1GHellhammer3045refit":{"primaryFactory":"Keystone,Pandora","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Hollis Mark X"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"VOX 340"},{"label":"Armor","manufacturer":"StarGuard IV"},{"label":"Communications","manufacturer":"HartfordCo COM 4000"},{"label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"HartfordCo XKZ 1"}],"manufacturer":"Earthwerks Incorporated,Red Devil Industries"},"BMBattleMaster_BLR1GHellhammer3053refit":{"primaryFactory":"Keystone,Pandora","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Hollis Mark X"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"VOX 340"},{"label":"Armor","manufacturer":"StarGuard IV"},{"label":"Communications","manufacturer":"HartfordCo COM 4000"},{"label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"HartfordCo XKZ 1"}],"manufacturer":"Earthwerks Incorporated,Red Devil Industries"},"BMBattleMaster_BLR1GHellhammer3059refit":{"primaryFactory":"Keystone,Pandora","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Hollis Mark X"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"VOX 340"},{"label":"Armor","manufacturer":"StarGuard IV"},{"label":"Communications","manufacturer":"HartfordCo COM 4000"},{"label":"Targeting/Tracking","manufacturer":"HartfordCo XKZ 1"}],"manufacturer":"Earthwerks Incorporated,Red Devil Induustries"},"BMBlackKnight_BL6KNTMordhau":{"primaryFactory":"Connaught","systems":[{"label":"Chassis/Frame","manufacturer":"Technicron 1L Endo Steel"},{"label":"Engine","manufacturer":"Vlar 300"